From: conda-forge maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Adapt jank's Clang facade to upstream CppInterOp 2.0.0

Keep fork-only reflection, overload diagnostics and interpreter setup in a
jank-owned facade. Delegate equivalent operations to the packaged library,
converting typed handles explicitly. Preserve array and reference semantics,
function-template lookup, qualified constructor lookup, embedded PCH files,
stale-PCH recovery and the large JIT code model.

The private interpreter bridge requires the exact upstream 2.0.0 headers
and matching LLVM headers. No forked CppInterOp library is built.

